  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Accuracy: useless. \"Never fraud\" scores 99.5% and catches nothing.\n",
    "# ROC-AUC: still misleading. Its x-axis is FPR = FP / (FP + TN), and with 99.5% negatives\n",
    "#   TN is enormous, so thousands of false positives barely move the FPR. The curve looks\n",
    "#   great while an analyst drowns in false alarms.\n",
    "# PR-AUC (average_precision): the honest one. Precision = TP / (TP + FP) has no TN term at\n",
    "#   all, so it can't be flattered by the majority class. Its baseline is the positive rate\n",
    "#   (0.005), so a PR-AUC of 0.3 is a 60x lift -- unimpressive-looking, actually excellent.\n",
    "# Report PR-AUC, plus recall at a fixed review budget (\"precision@top-100\"), which is what\n",
    "# the business actually operates on."
   ]
